<title>GREECE: Details on Greek personal income tax returns.</title>
<headline>Details on Greek personal income tax returns.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek income earners and pensioneers paid the lion's share in personal income taxes, 56.5 percent, in 1996 and farmers, fishermen and cattle breeders the least, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>					  Declared income  Tax	   %</p>
<p>					     (drachmas)  (drachmas) of tax</p>
<p>Total					10.8 trln    525.9  bln  100</p>
<p>Non-employed income earners	   482   bln    33   bln   5.3</p>
<p>Merchants, industrialists etc.	  2.2 trln  154   bln  24.7</p>
<p>Farmers, fishermen, cattle breeders 308   bln     7   bln   1.1</p>
<p>Income earners			    4.5   trln  257   bln  41.1</p>
<p>Self-employed			     574   bln    77.9 bln  12.4</p>
<p>Pensioneers				   2.1 trln   96.3 bln  15.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
